Subtract the common vertex $A$ from each endpoint:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\overrightarrow{AB}&=\langle-1-(-2),4-2,-3-0\rangle=\langle1,2,-3\rangle\\
\overrightarrow{AC}&=\langle-5-(-2),1-2,-1-0\rangle=\langle-3,-1,-1\rangle\\
\overrightarrow{AD}&=\langle-2-(-2),-1-2,0-0\rangle=\langle0,-3,0\rangle
\end{aligned}
$$

Use the scalar triple product:

$T=\overrightarrow{AB}\cdot(\overrightarrow{AC}\times\overrightarrow{AD})$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
T&=\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\ -3 & -1 & -1 \\ 0 & -3 & 0\end{vmatrix}
\end{aligned}
$$

Expand along row $3$, whose cofactor signs are $+,-,+$. Zero entries make no contribution. Evaluate the needed minors:

$$
\begin{aligned}
M_2&=\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\ -3 & -1\end{vmatrix}\\
&=1\cdot(-1)-(-3)\cdot(-3)=-10
\end{aligned}
$$

Combine the signed contributions before taking the absolute value:

$$
\begin{aligned}
T&=3M_2\\
&=3\cdot(-10)\\
&=(-30)=-30
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
\begin{aligned}
V&=|-30|=30\text{ cubic units}.
\end{aligned}
$$

