Substitute $x=- \frac{1}{2}$ and $y=-1$ throughout the expression. Keep parentheses around signed inputs:

$$
f(- \frac{1}{2},-1)=\frac{{e}^{(-1)}}{\arcsin\left(\left(- \frac{1}{2}\right)\right)}
$$

Evaluate the inner operations before combining them:

$$
\begin{aligned}
{e}^{(-1)} &=e^{-1} \\
\arcsin\left(\left(- \frac{1}{2}\right)\right) &=- \frac{\pi}{6} \\
\frac{{e}^{(-1)}}{\arcsin\left(\left(- \frac{1}{2}\right)\right)} &=- \frac{6}{e \pi}
\end{aligned}
$$

Thus $f(- \frac{1}{2},-1)=- \frac{6}{e \pi}$.
